    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The only test class in the project is `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files in that package are helpers), and its new `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` test \u2014 which asserts the `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` format \u2014 now passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a **per-city** sequence, keeping each piece of logic in its proper layer:\n\n- **`CustomerCodeGenerator`** (formatting logic) \u2014 `generate` now takes `city`, `lastName`, and the per-city owner count. Factored the shared 3-letter upper-casing into a small `prefix(...)` helper so CITY3 and LAST3 reuse the same code instead of duplicating it.\n- **`OwnerRepository`** (+ all three profile implementations: `SpringDataOwnerRepository`, `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl`, `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl`) \u2014 added a `countByCity(String)` query (case-insensitive, mirroring the existing `findByLastNameIgnoreCase` convention) so the sequence is \"one more than the owners already in that city.\" No existing count/query method covered this.\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 now passes `owner.getCity()` and `ownerRepository.countByCity(...)` into the generator.\n- **`membershipNumber`** \u2014 needed no code change; it's a `@Transient` value derived as `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `LON-SMI-0001-M26`).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode` description/example and the `membershipNumber` example to match.\n\nThe `customer_code` column is `VARCHAR(20)` (12-char codes fit), so no schema change was needed.",
